{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi Mr. ___, I'm Dr. ___. You're here today for your scheduled bronchoscopy and tracheostomy tube replacement, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that's right. I come in every month for the dilation because of the narrowing in my airway."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Given your Ruvalcaba-Myhre-Smith syndrome and relapsing polychondritis, these monthly procedures help keep your airway open."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right. Last time, things got a little scary with the unresponsiveness. I hope that doesn’t happen again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring you closely. The procedure went smoothly today. No complications during the bronchoscopy or balloon dilation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I do feel some soreness around the trach site, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. We’ll manage your pain with acetaminophen and ibuprofen. If it’s still uncomfortable, we can give you oxycodone as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I usually only need it the first day after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep it on hand. Also, we tried placing your custom trach tube today, but it got compressed, so we used a standard Portex 9 instead."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I remember that from last time. Is it safe to keep the Portex for now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s perfectly safe. We’ll plan for another attempt at the custom tube in a few weeks, once we reassess the anatomy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And the dilation—did it help open up the blockages?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We dilated the distal trachea up to 10 mm, the left mainstem to 9 mm, and the right side to 8 mm. There was some granulation tissue, which we gently removed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Was there bleeding?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The tissue was very fragile, but we controlled any minor bleeding with topical epinephrine. You’re stable now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve had issues with suctioning before—caused bleeding. I’d prefer to avoid that if possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2138-11-29 17:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Noted. We’ll rely on your cough to clear secretions unless absolutely necessary. Your lungs sound clear for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2138-11-30 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your chest X-ray from yesterday shows the trach is in place, no pneumothorax, and lung volumes have improved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2138-11-30 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. How’s my breathing looking?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2138-11-30 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on 40% oxygen via trach mask, saturating at 100%. No signs of distress. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2138-11-30 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been using my inhalers less. Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2138-11-30 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on scheduled tobramycin and fluticasone. I noticed you said you haven’t been using them regularly at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2138-11-30 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I forget sometimes. And the tobramycin wasn’t filled last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2138-11-30 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s important for preventing infections, especially with your history of Pseudomonas and other bacteria. Please restart it at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2138-11-30 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. I have an ID follow-up soon, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2138-11-30 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, with Dr. ___ this month. They’ll help keep your airway infections under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2138-11-30 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your repeat chest X-ray this morning shows no changes—trach is stable, no fluid or collapse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2138-11-30 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood work?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2138-11-30 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white count was a bit high yesterday—11.5—but it’s down to 8.5 today. That’s a good sign, no infection brewing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2138-11-30 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. My cough and shortness of breath at home haven’t changed, which is normal for me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2138-11-30 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your baseline is chronic cough and dyspnea. As long as it’s not worsening, we’re on track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2138-12-01 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made good progress. Pain is minimal, you’re off supplemental oxygen, and walking around fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2138-12-01 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2138-12-01 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if all stays stable. We’ll discharge you tomorrow morning. You’ll go home with a small supply of oxycodone for breakthrough pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2138-12-01 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just for a day or two?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2138-12-01 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, six tablets total—10 mg every four hours as needed. But stick to Tylenol and ibuprofen if possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2138-12-01 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I continue all my other meds—Esbriet, prednisone, losartan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2138-12-01 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. All your home medications are continued—Esbriet, prednisone, losartan, pantoprazole, and the inhalers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2138-12-01 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And rheumatology follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2138-12-01 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, with Dr. ___ to monitor your relapsing polychondritis. They’ll coordinate the next bronchoscopy in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2138-12-02 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Final check—your vitals are stable, lungs still clear, and you’re breathing comfortably."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2138-12-02 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m cleared to go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2138-12-02 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Continue all medications, avoid trach suctioning unless absolutely necessary, and follow up with rheumatology and ID."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2138-12-02 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if my breathing gets worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2138-12-02 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your team or go to the ER. But you’ve been stable post-procedure, so we expect continued improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2138-12-02 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, Doctor. I feel much better than last admission."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2138-12-02 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Glad to hear it. We’ll see you in clinic soon. Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2138-12-02 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2138-12-02 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming—your discharge paperwork is ready. You’re cleared to leave whenever you’re ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2138-12-02 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. I’ll get set up to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2138-12-02 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—we discussed the plan for a possible stent in the left mainstem bronchus in the future. That’s still on the table."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2138-12-02 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I remember. They measured it this time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2138-12-02 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, 4 cm in length. We’re considering an 8x40 or 10x30 stent later if needed. But for now, monthly dilation is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2138-12-02 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good to know. I’ll keep that in mind for follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2138-12-02 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your father is listed as your contact. We’ve gone over the discharge instructions with him too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2138-12-02 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, he’ll help me at home. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2138-12-02 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Stay well, and we’ll see you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2138-12-02 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, just one more question—should I worry if I cough up a little blood?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2138-12-02 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Minor streaking can happen due to the friable tissue. If it’s more than a few streaks or lasts more than a day, call us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2138-12-02 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks again."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2138-11-29 17:20:00",
    "admission_end": "2138-12-02 14:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for elective bronchoscopy with balloon dilation of the trachea and mainstem bronchi, along with tracheostomy tube replacement, due to recurrent tracheobronchial stenosis from Ruvalcaba-Myhre-Smith syndrome and relapsing polychondritis. The procedure was completed without complications, though the planned custom tracheostomy tube could not be placed due to compression and was replaced with a standard Portex 9 tube. Post-procedure, he experienced mild pain at the trach site, managed with acetaminophen, ibuprofen, and short-term oxycodone. He remained stable throughout the admission, with improving lung volumes on imaging and normalization of white blood cell count. He maintained oxygenation without distress and was discharged home on day three with instructions to continue all home medications, including inhaled tobramycin and fluticasone, and to follow up with rheumatology and infectious disease. Plans were made for future evaluation regarding possible stent placement in the left mainstem bronchus.",
    "problems": [
      "Other specified diseases of upper respiratory tract",
      "Other diseases of bronchus, not elsewhere classified",
      "Tracheostomy status",
      "Genetic carrier of other disease",
      "Other acute postprocedural pain",
      "Relapsing polychondritis",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Personal history of pneumonia (recurrent)",
      "Long term (current) use of systemic steroids",
      "Personal history of other infectious and parasitic diseases"
    ]
  }
}
